flint build: build the project's executable

Usage:
  flint build [options]

  The executable is out/<profile>/<name>. What it was built from stays in out/ too, so
  the next build only redoes what changed.

Options:
  --release            the 'release' profile: optimized
  --profile=<name>     a profile of flint.toml; debug (the default) and release always exist
  -v, --verbose        show the commands that are run (the C compiler, flintc)
  --color=<when>       colored output: auto (default), always or never
  -h, --help           show this help

Examples:
  flint build
  flint build --release         (out/release/<name>)
